From 54ce8d8d88561dfcc44c1a4f1f14cbe9dcd735ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <alexander@auralite.local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:59:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] X1 sandbox
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second EXEC phase: the runtime half of the verifier. aura-exec gains its
first external dependency — the engine.

- aura_exec::sandbox: size -> X0 census -> compile -> zero-import check ->
  instantiate with store limits -> call run -> closed trap set. Every step
  can only reject.
- SandboxLimits::restrictive(): fuel 1,000,000; memory 4096 pages; module
  512 KiB; stack 512 KiB; trace 4096 events; validate() refuses anything
  looser than the published census ceiling.
- Engine trait + two backends from one configuration: wasmi =2.0.0
  (default, portable dispatch + deterministic) and wasmtime =50.0.0
  (feature wasmtime-engine). Execution { outcome, fuel_used, trace,
  exports }, SandboxError (7 variants), TrapKind (6).
- DoD gate: 19 programs — 6 executed, 5 trapped, 8 refused; fuel pinned
  per program by cargo run -p aura-exec --bin x1-record.
- Cross-engine (measured): wasmtime agrees with wasmi on all 19 outcomes.
- Three defects found by the new gates and fixed here: missing wasmi
  dispatch feature (loop { br 0 } overflowed the native stack instead of
  consuming fuel), an under-specified trap classifier, and a
  component-model/reference-types conflict that made wasmtime reject
  every module.
- 6 negative controls -> 116 total; 144 new external crates in the lock
  (wasmi 10, optional wasmtime 134).

Measured: 193 Rust tests, 4,532 vectors in 19 fixtures, 116 NC,
239 external crates, 0 validators / 0 blocks / 0 transactions.
